    "module/compact/summary": {
      "by": 3,
      "depends_on": [
        "tokenbudget.estimate"
      ],
      "exports": [
        "head_tail(text: str, budget: int, head_frac: float = 0.6) -> str",
        "drop_oldest(messages: list[dict], budget: int) -> list[dict]",
        "ELISION_MARKER"
      ],
      "module": "compact",
      "notes": [
        "head_tail bisects the retained character count so the result exactly saturates the budget as measured by estimate.count_tokens; the retained slice is provably maximal",
        "marker is ELISION_MARKER = chr(10)+\"...[elided]...\"+chr(10) (4 tokens); if the budget cannot even fit the marker, head_tail returns the empty string",
        "head_frac splits the retained characters: head gets int(keep*head_frac), the tail gets the rest; head is a real prefix and tail a real suffix of the input",
        "drop_oldest never mutates its input and always keeps the last message, even when that message alone exceeds the budget",
        "negative budget raises ValueError; head_frac outside [0.0,1.0] raises ValueError"
      ],
